/ActualText (Twelve line graphs in a 3x4 grid showing log\(MDS\) and log\(MSE\) against the number of subsamples across different methods. The figure contains twelve line graphs organized in a 3x4 grid, showcasing the relationship between the number of subsamples \(500 to 2500\) and both log\(MDS\) and log\(MSE\) values. Each graph includes panels labeled from R1,M1 to R3,M5, with different methods represented, including FULL, UNIF, LEV, IF, MCD, and SPAR. Generally, both log\(MDS\) and log\(MSE\) show decreasing trends as the number of subsamples increases, indicating improved performance with higher subsamples. The y-axis values range from approximately -12.5 to -7.5 for log\(MDS\) and vary for log\(MSE\). Each graph features distinct line styles for different methods, allowing for comparisons of performance across the models.)
