/Alt (A grid of 28 graphs: 16 line graphs for log\(PMSE\) across subsamples and 12 scatter plots for log\(p-values\) across subsamples, showing trends for multiple methods. The figure features 28 individual graphs arranged in a 4x4 grid for log\(PMSE\) and a 4x3 grid for log\(p-values\). The log\(PMSE\) plots show the y-axis with varying ranges, where 'FULL' method generally shows the lowest values among six methods \(FULL, UNIF, LEV, IF, MCD, SPAR\). The x-axis represents the number of subsamples from 1 to 8. The log\(p-values\) plots display varying negative values on the y-axis and trends generally decreasing with increasing subsamples. Different methods are represented by distinct line styles or markers across both sets of graphs. Variability is noted, particularly in slopes and performance across the combinations of C and M conditions for both metrics.)
>>
